# S vs Kotlin — Comparison Sheet (S 3.0.0 FREEZE)

Updated: 2026-10-17 · S Version 3.0.0

## 1. Positioning

| | **S** | **Kotlin** |
|---|--------|------------|
| Tagline | Simple · Safe · Supreme | Concise · Safe · Interoperable |
| Maturity | Early / research → usable offline core | Production, industry standard |
| Primary home | Own interpreter + SVM + tools | JVM / Android / Multiplatform |
| Goal | Learn fast, ship sealed .sbx, one command | App & server scale, huge ecosystem |

## 2. Language surface

| Feature | S 3.0.0 | Kotlin |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Variables | `let` / `var` | `val` / `var` |
| Null / absence | `opt`, `some`/`none`, `??`, `?.` | `T?`, `?.`, `?:`, `!!` |
| Functions | `fn` | `fun` |
| Classes | `class`, `new`, `this` | `class`, constructors |
| Lambdas | `{ x -> ... }` | `{ x -> ... }` |
| Pipe | `\|>` | mostly library / not built-in |
| When / match | `when` | `when` (richer) |
| Guard / early exit | `guard` | early `return` |
| Defer | `defer` | `try/finally` / `use` |
| Async | `async` / `await` / `spawn` (cooperative) | coroutines (mature) |
| Collections | list, map + map/filter/sort | rich stdlib |
| Modules | `use` / `use x as y` | packages + imports |
| Errors | `safe/rescue`, `result` ok/err, `require` | exceptions + Result libs |
| String interp | `"Hello, $name!"` | `"Hello, $name"` |
| Multiline string | `"""..."""` | `"""..."""` |

**S wins (ergonomics):** pipe `|>`, `defer`, simpler beginner surface, one-file mental model.  
**Kotlin wins (depth):** coroutines, sealed hierarchies, full type system, generics, multiplatform.

## 3. Safety

| Topic | S | Kotlin |
|-------|---|--------|
| Null safety | Runtime `opt` + `s check` rules | Compile-time nullable types |
| Contracts | `require`, `assert`, `guard` | `require`, `check`, contracts |
| Immutability | `let` + `freeze` / strict_let | `val` + read-only collections |
| Memory | Host GC (no manual free) | JVM/Native GC or RC |
| Static analysis | OptChecker (growing) | Compiler + IDE inspections |

**Kotlin still stronger** on compile-time null safety.  
**S** is improving via `s check` + fail-closed Shield.

## 4. Tooling

| Tool | S | Kotlin |
|------|---|--------|
| Run | `s run` | `kotlinc` / Gradle / IDE |
| Check | `s check` | compiler |
| Test | `s test` (114+) | JUnit / kotlin.test |
| Format | `s fmt` (minimal) | ktlint / IntelliJ |
| REPL | `s repl` | `kotlin` REPL |
| Bytecode VM | `s vm` (own SVM) | JVM bytecode |
| Packages | `s hub` + `s.lock` | Maven/Gradle |
| Project new | `s new` | Android Studio / wizards |
| Release | `s release` → `.sbx` | APK/AAB/JAR |
| LSP | goto-def, rename, complete, diagnostics | Excellent (IDEA) |

## 5. Ship & protection

| | S | Kotlin/Android |
|---|---|----------------|
| Release artifact | `.sbx` (encrypted + stripped) | APK/AAB (R8/ProGuard) |
| Own crypto layer | S Shield SBX2 (PBKDF2, dual HMAC) | R8 + optional commercial |
| Plain source in release | Policy: no | Often stripped/obfuscated |
| Reverse engineering | Harder casual RE; not impossible | Same industry reality |

## 6. Performance & deploy

| | S | Kotlin |
|---|---|--------|
| Speed | Interpreter / Python-host limited | JVM JIT / Native strong |
| Single binary | Not yet | Possible (Native) |
| Android production | Scaffold / stub path | First-class |
| Server | Possible via host | Excellent |

## 7. LOC feel (benchmarks folder)

Typical small scripts: **S often fewer lines** (hello, pipe chain, list unique).  
Large apps: **Kotlin ecosystem wins** (libraries, UI, concurrency).

## 8. When to choose which

**Choose S if you want:**
- Fast learning, few concepts
- Offline core + one CLI (`s`)
- Sealed `.sbx` ship with own Shield
- Experimentation / teaching / small tools

**Choose Kotlin if you want:**
- Production Android or large JVM backend
- Mature coroutines + libraries
- Hiring market + long-term vendor support
- Compile-time null safety guarantees

## 9. Scorecard (honest, S 3.0.0)

| Category | Edge |
|----------|------|
| Beginner simplicity | **S** |
| Syntax ergonomics (pipe/defer) | **S** |
| Type / null safety depth | **Kotlin** |
| Concurrency | **Kotlin** |
| Performance | **Kotlin** |
| Ecosystem | **Kotlin** |
| Own sealed release story | **S** |
| IDE maturity | **Kotlin** |
| Offline single-toolchain joy | **S** |

## 10. One line

> **S is the simple sealed offline core; Kotlin is the industrial platform.**  
> S 3.0.0 is usable and tested — not a Kotlin replacement for large production Android yet.
